cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Research compendium for "Mapping the AI Research of China, the US and the EU:
  A Scientometric Analysis of Citation Shares within AI Subdisciplines
  (2020-2024)"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the compendium and
  the associated article.
type: software
version: 3.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Pigeon-Effect/qss_publication
abstract: >-
  Research compendium for a scientometric analysis of citation shares within AI
  subdisciplines, based on 1,986,659 AI-related publications from 2020-2024
  retrieved from OpenAlex. It contains the complete pipeline: keyword
  construction from 125 survey papers into 279 search terms, OpenAlex
  retrieval, quality control, a hierarchical, semi-supervised document
  clustering (SPECTER embeddings, K-Means over-segmentation, human
  consolidation) yielding 5 domains, 31 fields and 106 research fronts, a test
  of how faithfully the full corpus inherits the sample clustering, fractional
  citation shares of China, the United States and the EU-27 across that
  taxonomy, and the figures. The taxonomy is validated externally by an
  LLM-based document-intrusion test adapted from Chang et al. (2009); the
  compendium includes the complete record of all 3,000 trials, a paired prompt
  experiment, the Supplementary Information with bloc citation shares for every
  cluster, and the manuscript.
keywords:
  - scientometrics
  - topic modeling
  - cluster validation
  - intrusion detection
  - large language models
  - OpenAlex
  - artificial intelligence
  - citation analysis

